findings.proof_of_concept:
@dev: "Use `lookback = 0` for the instantaneous price. `lookback > 0` for a TWAP."
Actual code: return lookback > 0 ? getPrice(priceAggregatorAddress, maxTimeout) : getTwap(priceAggregatorAddress, maxTimeout, lookback);
// lookback>0 path -> getPrice (SPOT, not TWAP); lookback==0 path -> getTwap(...,0) -> final `.div(lookback)` = `.div(0)` -> revert (not the documented 0 sentinel)

@notice: "migrates `amount` of Beans to L2, issued to `reciever`."
Actual code:
  uint256 constant EXTERNAL_L1_BEANS = 0;
  ...
  s.sys.migration.migratedL1Beans += amount;
  require(EXTERNAL_L1_BEANS >= s.sys.migration.migratedL1Beans, "L2Migration: exceeds maximum migrated"); // 0 >= amount -> always reverts for amount>0
  C.bean().mint(reciever, amount); // unreachable

